      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nThe CPU INT4 W4A8 linear path and the x86 grouped-gemm MoE experts are gated on\r\n`torch.cpu._is_amx_tile_supported()`. That check is stricter than what the kernels\r\nactually need, so AVX-512 BF16 CPUs without AMX tiles (AMD Zen 4/Zen 5) never\r\nselect them:\r\n\r\n- `CPUWNA16LinearKernel.process_weights_after_loading` clears `layer.use_w4a8`, so\r\n  every INT4 linear falls back to `cpu_gemm_wna16` even with the default\r\n  `VLLM_CPU_INT4_W4A8=1`.\r\n- `CPUExpertsInt4`, `CPUExpertsInt8` and `X86CPUUnquantizedExperts` report\r\n  `_supports_current_device() == False`.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
